Models separate inputs, calculations, and outputs with consistent units and signs.|A hard-coded tax assumption sits in a labelled input cell.|Why separate assumptions?|Traceability and controlled changes|To remove all uncertainty|To avoid documentation
Historical preparation standardises audited data, policies, units, and non-recurring items.|₹ crore data mixed with ₹ lakh creates a hundredfold error.|First check…?|Units and reconciliations|Only chart colours|Only growth rates
Three-statement models link earnings, balance-sheet changes, and cash.|Closing cash from cash flow becomes balance-sheet cash.|A balancing cash plug alone proves correctness?|No|Yes|Only if assets equal liabilities
Revenue and cost schedules translate operational drivers into earnings.|Units 100 × price ₹5 gives revenue ₹500.|Volume 120 at unchanged price gives…?|₹600|₹500|₹125
Working-capital schedules forecast operating balances from sales, costs, and days.|Higher receivable days ties up additional cash.|All else equal, higher receivable days lowers…?|Free cash flow|Revenue necessarily|Depreciation
Fixed-asset schedules track additions, depreciation, disposals, and impairment.|PPE ₹100 + capex ₹20 − depreciation ₹10 closes at ₹110.|Closing PPE is…?|₹110|₹130|₹90
Debt schedules link draws, repayments, interest, and liquidity.|Debt ₹100 + draw ₹20 − repayment ₹30 closes at ₹90.|Interest should ordinarily depend on…?|Relevant outstanding debt and timing|Sales only|Closing equity only
Tax and equity schedules distinguish cash tax, accounting tax, earnings, owner flows, and shares.|Retained earnings ₹50 + profit ₹10 − dividends ₹3 closes at ₹57.|Closing retained earnings is…?|₹57|₹63|₹40
Circularity occurs when calculations depend on each other; balancing checks identify inconsistent flows.|Interest affects cash, while a cash shortfall affects borrowing and interest.|Best response?|Design controlled circularity or a justified non-circular approximation|Hide the imbalance|Add unexplained assets
Scenarios change linked assumptions; sensitivities isolate selected inputs.|Base, downside, and upside forecasts use coherent driver sets.|A downside scenario should change…?|Economically related assumptions|Only the scenario label|Only formatting
DCF models price expected cash; comparable models apply justified peer multiples.|FCFF pairs with WACC; equity earnings multiples pair with equity value.|EV divided by net profit is automatically a consistent multiple?|No|Yes|Only for debt-free firms
Acquisition models combine funding, earnings, purchase accounting, synergies, and integration costs.|A deal adds earnings but also financing interest and extra amortisation.|EPS uplift alone proves positive deal NPV?|No|Yes|Only for cash deals
LBO models forecast debt service and equity exit proceeds under leverage.|₹100 enterprise exit value less ₹40 debt leaves ₹60 equity before other adjustments.|Equity proceeds are…?|₹60|₹100|₹140
Project and property models track construction, operations, debt, reserves, and contractual waterfalls.|Construction spending precedes rental or project revenue.|Ignoring construction timing mainly understates…?|Funding needs and timing risk|Only tax labels|Only share count
Sector models adapt drivers to banking, insurance, and startup economics.|Banks model loans and capital; startups model burn and runway.|One generic industrial model fits all sectors without changes?|No|Yes|Only at equal revenue
Model audits check identities, signs, links, formulas, and assumptions independently.|A balance check passes while a formula references the wrong period.|This shows…?|One check is insufficient|The model is correct|Documentation is unnecessary
